  "notes": [
    "Each repeat uses a fresh cache tag, so vLLM's persistent prefix cache cannot carry between repeats; within a repeat all N agents share one tag (and thus the shared prefix) and the first-scheduled request cold-prefills it while the rest ride the copy-on-write cache.",
    "vLLM is restarted between arms (one arm per invocation), so no prefix-cache state carries between raw and compile.",
    "peak gauges are sampled at ~25 ms (may miss faster transients); running/waiting are vLLM scheduler gauges, kv_cache_usage_perc is the fixed KV-cache metric."
